 14 points.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e87c75538b72f9b2\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa0667d896ef3d7b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa0667d896ef3d7b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b94303d69d7a6302\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b94303d69d7a6302\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1bf61271bfcc1629\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1bf61271bfcc1629\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"adcd2d84c745367c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nProcess (NAEP). 2022 Mathematics Assessment. The decline in mathematics scores in the eighth grade is more significant, as <strong>10 states fell below the national average</strong> · (274). Virginia (279) was the only state to score above the national average.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"adcd2d84c745367c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba516ae28991e087\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba516ae28991e087\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n  